FRD_Cursor_Transition.md
1. Current SQL Schema
The foundational PostgreSQL database running on Supabase relies on a normalized Double-Ledger architecture. The active tables and their key relationships are:
entidades: Stores the network of users (roles: ADMIN, DST, LOC, SOCIO). Includes tracking for geographical zones, custom commission percentages (base, local, logistics), and a self-referencing foreign key (id_padre) to establish hierarchy.
cuentas_financieras: Manages company routing accounts (e.g., Cash, Personal, Enterprise). Links to entidades via id_entidad and defines the strict tax rules applied to revenue via the tipo_fiscalidad column (LIBRE, IVA_ONLY, FULL_TAX).
catalogo_productos: Centralizes both raw materials (INSUMO) and finished goods (TERMINADO).
listas_precios: Establishes geographic pricing. Links to catalogo_productos (id_producto) and dictates final retail prices specific to zones (Zacatecas vs. Foráneo).
recetas_produccion: Bill of Materials (BOM) lookup table. Links finished products (id_producto_terminado) to required raw materials (id_insumo) using a DECIMAL(10,4) type for strict fractional requirements.
inventario_ledger (also instantiated as inventario_mov): The source of truth for stock. Tracks all physical movements (ENTRADA, SALIDA, MERMA, PRODUCCION), linked to catalogo_productos and cross-referenced with entidades for origin and destination routing.
transacciones_tickets: The master sales receipt table. Records transactions linking id_vendedor and id_comprador to entidades, and maps funds to a destination account via id_cuenta_destino. It stores pure catalog subtotal, real collected amounts, and reverse-calculated tax withholdings.
ticket_detalles: Child table for the POS cart. Maps multiple SKUs to a single id_ticket master record.
finanzas_ledger: The monetary source of truth. Records all cash flow movements across cuentas_financieras. It handles manual adjustments, debt payments, and automatically logs operational expenses like "Subsidio Fiscal".
feed_actividad: A lightweight notification timeline table tracking events (id_entidad_actora, tipo_evento) into human-readable strings via pre-formatted templates.
2. Implemented Core Logic
The application enforces strict backend isolation for business math to avoid client-side state failures.
Reverse Math (IVA/IEPS): Completely operational. The system calculates base income and exact tax burdens dynamically, reversing the math from a catalog's tax-inclusive final price. If an enterprise account triggers an IVA/IEPS burden (e.g., 16% IVA and 53% IEPS), the POS calculates this in real-time. Furthermore, the app automates "Fuga Fiscal" (Fiscal Leakage) by generating transparent ledger expenses whenever the company absorbs tax burdens on behalf of distributor debt payments.
Fractional BOM (láminas de plata): Operational. Inventory logic securely deducts manufacturing components using deep decimals (DECIMAL(10,4)). For instance, bottling 50 units of 50ml product mathematically deducts exactly 3.33 units of silver sheets alongside integral deductions of bottles, caps, and labels without rounding errors.
Commission Cascade (Cascada de Comisiones): Operational. Built into the POS engine to manage the multi-level distribution network. When a Local sub-node (LOC) processes a sale, the system checks for a parent Distributor (DST) and calculates passive income using the precise formula (comision_hijo_local + comision_base_local) - comision_base. This generates an immediate, automated ABONO_DEUDA on the parent's ledger.
3. Completed UI Views
The Next.js App Router integrates Server Components with targeted Client Components for robust interfaces.
Point of Sale (POS): Functional multi-SKU cart interface. Includes dynamic pricing adjustments based on the buyer's geographic zone, an automated anonymous buyer bypass ("Público en General"), Real-Time Reverse Math tax breakdowns, and thermal-receipt generation designed for WhatsApp sharing.
Dynamic Account Statement (Estado de Cuenta): Operational. A per-distributor ledger (/dashboard/distribuidores/[id]) showing generated debt, applied payments, aging timelines, and unified historical activity. Features dual-action transaction routing (money/payments vs. physical returns).
Finance Dashboard: Operational. Uses React Server Components to digest finanzas_ledger data entirely on the server. Renders global income, operational expenses, net balance KPI cards, and a color-coded chronological transaction table.
Inventory Dashboard: Operational. Serves as a command center analyzing inventario_ledger. Shows real-time aggregated product stock using entry/exit formulas, triggers replenishment warnings for stock <= 10, and features a dedicated module for registering physical production to trigger the BOM engine.
Network Dashboard (Directorio/Red): Operational. Lists all connected entities mapped out by roles (DST/LOC), actively cross-referencing id_padre in local memory to display hierarchy without complex server-side JOIN failures. Displays KPIs for network scale and direct routing to individual account statements.
4. Security Architecture
The application relies on Supabase Auth combined with Next.js structural gating.
The "Wall of Fog" (Muro de Niebla): Fully implemented. The SOCIO role operates under strict global read-only constraints. Route protection immediately ejects SOCIO or unauthorized accounts attempting to access mutation routes (e.g., /pos, /nuevo). On the frontend, mutation buttons (+ Nuevo Movimiento, Ir al POS) are conditionally hidden from view based on the role. Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) acts as a secondary failsafe, explicitly blocking INSERT, UPDATE, or DELETE commands from this role.
Role-Based Menu Blindness: When a standard DST logs into the platform, Next.js routing intentionally obscures the Finance and Inventory tabs in the UI, locking them solely into their own account statements to prevent data leaks from the parent enterprise.
5. Immediate Backlog
According to the exact project boundary established at the end of Conversation 6, the system transitions into Phase 7 focusing strictly on two major architectural modules:
Recurrent Billing & Pending Payments (Cobros Recurrentes & Abonos Pendientes): Building a "vault of trust" allowing distributors to submit payments that remain marked as "Pending" until an administrator manually verifies and accepts the physical bank transfer or cash.
Global "Power BI" Filters (Filtro "Power BI" de Fechas Globales): Implementing top-level date range selection within the UI layout to dynamically recalculate and filter all financial graphs, inventory totals, and network tables in real-time across the Dashboards (the "Final Boss" of the current development phase).
